+# Initial source-buffer REPL (development preview)
+
+On a terminal, run `ffort.exe` without a source filename to enter the REPL.
+The common CLI is also built as `fortfront-interpreter` by FPM; this feature does
+not change the existing Windows executable naming workflow.
+
+`--repl` (alias `--interactive`) forces a session when standard input is a pipe.
+Without a filename or either flag, nonterminal stdin is a complete batch source,
+not an interactive transcript. `--nologo` hides the banner; `--prompt TEXT`
+changes the prompt (up to 128 printable characters, including an empty prompt).
+`--max-steps N` sets each explicit run's budget. REPL mode does not accept a
+filename, `--check`, or registered `--input` bindings. Those remain batch options.
+
+## First supported increment
+
+Enter standard Fortran declarations and executable statements for one program
+body. The buffer is wrapped in `program repl_session`, `implicit none`, and
+`end program repl_session`. Declarations must precede executable statements.
+
+- `.` or `.run`: compile and execute the entire buffer with fresh runtime state.
+- `.list`: display the effective standard Fortran source, including the wrapper.
+- `.clear`: discard the buffer and clear the last error.
+- `.help`: describe commands and limits.
+- `.quit` or `.quit!`: leave without executing or saving.
+
+There is no automatic execution. Source checks occur on explicit run, so an
+incomplete block can be entered over several lines. A failed run keeps the
+buffer; completing the block and explicitly running again starts fresh. EOF
+never implicitly executes or saves. Each deliberate `.run` repeats the program's
+effects; this is not incremental execution. The session returns the last error
+status until a successful run or `.clear`.
+
+Example:
+
+```text
+> integer :: n
+> n = 2
+> print *, n*n
+> .run
+4
+> .quit
+```
+
+## Boundaries and differences from ofort
+
+This implements the initial deferred source-buffer workflow, not all of ofort's
+interactive features. Full program/module input, load/save, editing commands,
+autorun, auto-end, declaration reordering, `let`/`const`, expression queries and
+`.vars` are not implemented. In particular, queries are not simulated by replaying
+past statements: doing so would duplicate output, random-number and input effects.
+A persistent runtime session is separate future work. Unlike ofort's normal
+quit path, neither quit command writes an automatic save file.
+
+The source remains subject to the interpreter's existing supported Fortran
+subset. Session input is bounded to 4,096 bytes per line, 10,000 body lines, and
+1,048,576 source bytes including the wrapper. An overlong input record is fully
+discarded so its remainder cannot become a command. NUL-containing lines are
+rejected. Batch stdin has the existing 1 MiB source limit.
+
+Current validation uses Linux GNU Fortran 14.2 plus real PTY transcripts. Windows
+console detection uses `_isatty`/`_fileno`, but source portability is not a claim
+that Windows execution has been tested. This preview is not the separately
+certified 0.56 delivery and has not yet received full maintained-suite certification.
